: \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fae341ada5046f640235dfe9011e50fb71bf4143d515732ab3d7cea29df11e68","event_uuid":"5c7acae1-7e16-4eea-9be8-8bfda01041c6","position":{"commit_sha":"ccb492ab77017726647dbf8d5d74084ceb8cc6c6","position":"1787705339460532001-5c7acae1-7e16-4eea-9be8-8bfda01041c6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8332fe980993a6b0bb9007ec732885a29fc855c70b854f171049a09a462d132e","event_uuid":"7bae0f1e-be7b-4b32-a951-1d1c0b376393","position":{"commit_sha":"c5522784d1b35670f3d7dd93ef274f177a99851b","position":"1787708324259172148-7bae0f1e-be7b-4b32-a951-1d1c0b376393"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"73a10058cf0d61e7b312268dd2ab7cab275fdaa3e7613f0efdfc98f365c2e14d","event_uuid":"c6f5ad8a-d7d1-46a0-9f17-ee9c9cc18fb5","position":{"commit_sha":"cda3c9b4e88d9bdaed5da604a882abc906e80399","position":"1787710396839211390-c6f5ad8a-d7d1-46a0-9f17-ee9c9cc18fb5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation static review complete. The patch now includes the lazy OID-pinned ticket view, predicate receipt replay, and isolated three-event completion-close publication. Static scrutiny found and corrected three issues before review: frozen receipt tuples were normalized before replay, child-closure evidence no longer widens field-only predicates to exact child states and preserves archived-child parity, and inbound-link discovery now covers legacy alias, short-id, and Jira LINK targets. The 40-path file-impact manifest now exactly matches the worktree. git diff --check, module-size checks, and production semantic diagnostics pass; local tests, lint, typecheck, compilation, and gates were intentionally not run per the operator CI-only instruction.","timestamp":1787701159147809001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fresh plan review PASS signed at code SHA 3ea0bed5acb4 with zero blocking findings (total 231.6s). Advisory dispositions: T5b fixed in scope because delivery commits only in a UUID-private candidate before push; exhausted transport/auth/outage retries raise and discard that candidate, while only a proven remote acceptance can produce a local-pending state. T9 fixed in scope because the process resolver cache is capped at two OID/schema entries and the raw-link index is owned and discarded by one pinned view. P4 accepted because the 40 paths form one indivisible stable-read plus atomic-publication vertical slice whose transaction contracts cross those seams. P6 accepted because the implementation adds focused observable-behavior suites and explicit CI verify commands even though the original high-level AC lines group related predicates. No plan text was changed, so the signed PASS remains current.","timestamp":1787701861513498001}],"created_at":1787679134292977001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0bca6d10-c4df-45d7-9f3a-aab5f535ca06","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"99cd-e61b-bc64-48af"},{"link_uuid":"00ef076a-77ea-42be-bfee-fe28f6016478","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"831f-326d-be85-437a"},{"link_uuid":"0868f642-3b93-409f-aedb-4d154195ff8d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7dea-2f00-db57-4a96"},{"link_uuid":"39722339-a6fd-43e7-87ec-39d3cde06aa1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1ee2-9704-4f59-45f1"},{"link_uuid":"e026ad2a-569a-4c34-92e3-6f8676bf8208","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"14fe-9b7b-c46b-46e0"},{"link_uuid":"c3a34f99-bb44-42f1-a3a4-7434af23835c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5866-1024-54af-4fd8"},{"link_uuid":"7bae0f1e-be7b-4b32-a951-1d1c0b376393","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"aca9-a41d-2449-45b0"},{"link_uuid":"c6f5ad8a-d7d1-46a0-9f17-ee9c9cc18fb5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"692a-6b1b-05c8-4d21"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nCompletion verification currently materializes the full Git-backed ticket store although a run reads only a small subset. Close traces attributed 135-235 seconds to this phase. Approved research on `shaven-censorable-sifaka` measured the real store: tracker-OID capture was 9.5 ms p50, tree/object reads about 11 ms p50, and fetching plus uncached reduction of one real ticket was 29.156 ms for 10 files / 62,426 bytes with exact state-hash parity. Revision A stayed byte-identical after a normal rebar write advanced the live tracker to B.\n\nThe close path also publishes PASS `COMPLETION_VERDICT`, closing `STATUS`, and completion `SIGNATURE` through separate writes. A durable PASS can outlive a failed close, and a closed ticket can outlive a failed signature. We need one stable read basis and one atomic publication boundary.\n\n## Contract\n- `code_oid` is resolved once from `--ref`; `tickets_oid` independently identifies tracker state. Typed interfaces must prevent swapping them.\n- The ticket view reads Git objects lazily at `tickets_oid`, never falls back to live state, and never writes caches inside the view.\n- The read receipt records exact tickets, negative reads, direct-child membership, transitive descendants, inbound/outbound relations and consulted reachability, plus global resolver inputs such as `.bridge_state/bindings.json`.\n- Atomic means one committed-store transaction contains PASS sidecar, closed STATUS, and completion SIGNATURE, or none is committed and HEAD/index/worktree return to their prior state. OID-pinned readers see the complete old or complete new commit.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add a pinned-ticket reader backed by `ls-tree`, batched `cat-file`, and the existing uncached reducer input seam. Resolve arbitrary IDs/aliases/Jira bindings at `tickets_oid`; record not-found as a negative read. Put derived resolver/graph indexes outside the immutable tree and key them by tracker OID plus schema version. Unsupported broad queries fail closed.\n2. Thread this view through completion context assembly, deterministic ticket checks, and agent ticket tools. Keep code reads on the separate code snapshot. Bug `shimmery-customary-dorking` will experimentally test the suspected live-code gap; this story preserves typed separation without assuming that hypothesis is true.\n3. Before mutation, validate the receipt from A against current descendant Tn. Reject non-ancestor history. Diff changed ticket/global paths and recompute affected predicates at both endpoints. Unrelated changes may continue; an exact, hierarchy, link, negative, or resolver conflict discards the verdict and restarts at Tn.\n4. Outside the write lock, prepare the verdict, receipt digest, completion certificate payload, event UUIDs, and all work not requiring final HLC order. Each run owns `(run_id, code_oid, tickets_oid, receipt_digest)` and unique temporary paths.\n5. Extend the status transaction to accept three prepared close events. Inside the lock, assert tracker HEAD still equals validated Tn and root status remains `in_progress`; finalize HLC/parent linkage/authorship, stage all three, and make one local Git commit. Any signing, staging, index, or commit fault rolls back only this bundle and restores pre-operation state. Preserve reducer/event compatibility.\n6. Release the lock before ordinary fast-forward push. On rejection, fetch and revalidate: rebuild/retry an unrelated delta or restart verification for a relevant delta. Never force a ref update or push. A same-ticket race is idempotent only when the existing close binds an equivalent code OID, receipt, and attestation; a loser leaves no PASS sidecar.\n7. Measure ticket-OID capture, lazy reads/reduction, receipt validation, bundle preparation, lock wait/hold, local commit, and push/retry. Metrics add only constant-time timestamps inside the lock. Document the receipt vocabulary, atomicity boundary, retries, rollout, and separate code/ticket revisions.\n\n## Rollout / Back-out\nPut the new completion path behind one configuration switch and retain the legacy path as an explicit operator back-out during dogfooding. Selection is fixed and recorded at operation start; a run never silently falls back after capturing `tickets_oid`. Default enablement is separate and evidence-based. The mechanism is in-process and CI-provider-independent.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Given tracker A and later normal write B, a run pinned to A returns byte/state-identical ticket reads while live writes continue, without materializing the full ticket tree.\n- [ ] Any ticket requested at runtime loads from A and extends the receipt; missing returns not-found-at-A plus a negative dependency, never live fallback.\n- [ ] Direct/transitive hierarchy and inbound/outbound relation predicates invalidate on relevant create/remove/reparent/relink changes; a proven unrelated mutation remains valid.\n- [ ] Alias/Jira/global binding resolution is pinned to A; relevant binding changes invalidate. Unsupported queries fail closed.\n- [ ] Completion code evidence remains bound to separately resolved `code_oid`; tests reject swapped code/ticket roots.\n- [ ] LLM work, lazy reads, receipt validation, preparation, and push occur outside the write lock. Only final HEAD/status assertions, ordering/signing, staging, and one commit are inside; wait/hold are measured.\n- [ ] A successful close creates exactly one local commit containing PASS `COMPLETION_VERDICT`, `STATUS in_progress -> closed`, and completion `SIGNATURE`, all bound to one run/code/receipt identity.\n- [ ] Fault injection at signing, staging, index, and commit boundaries leaves prior HEAD/status and no committed sidecar/signature; retry creates at most one equivalent bundle.\n- [ ] Two parallel reviews cannot publish mixed artifacts: one wins; the loser recognizes an equivalent close or restarts without leaving PASS. Unrelated reviews may both commit after revalidation.\n- [ ] Non-ancestor state, relevant receipt drift, and remote fast-forward rejection fail closed without force; unrelated descendant deltas can revalidate/retry.\n- [ ] Derived caches are OID/schema-keyed with per-run temporaries and do not write inside the pinned view.\n- [ ] Focused lazy-read parity, hierarchy/link phantom, negative-read, resolver, cross-process concurrency, and rollback tests pass in CI, followed by project lint, typecheck, and test gates.\n- [ ] Documentation covers the stable-read contract, full receipt vocabulary, committed-store atomicity, rollout/back-out, remote-writer limitation, and metric phases.\n\n## Out of Scope\n- Replacing Git or reducing the lock to `git update-ref` while the mutable checkout remains authoritative.\n- Acting on either unproven bug (`shimmery-customary-dorking`, `lineny-barathea-ladybug`) before its experiment.\n- Setting a lock-duration SLO before instrumentation produces a distribution.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/0005-snapshot-cache-architecture.md","reason":"Record the lazy ticket OID view and receipt-checked atomic close decision."},{"path":"docs/concurrency.md","reason":"Document stable-read predicates, lock width, retries, and publication boundaries."},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"Document the default-off completion_pinned_ticket_view rollout switch."},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"Document completion read modes, receipt vocabulary, atomic delivery, and timing fields."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_autoresume.py","reason":"Reuse one pinned ticket view across verifier auto-resume attempts and avoid incompatible legacy PASS reuse."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py","reason":"Capture one ticket OID before completion checks and route deterministic reads through it."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","reason":"Select and report the receipt-bearing atomic completion bundle."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/txn.py","reason":"Prepare a final STATUS event under an existing close transaction lock."},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"Add the typed experimental rollout configuration field."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py","reason":"Allow commit-reference resolution against the pinned ticket resolver."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py","reason":"Bind the current immutable ticket view and propagate pinned read failures."},{"path":"src/rebar/_reads.py","reason":"Route modeled library reads through the pinned view and reject unsupported live fallbacks."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/event_append.py","reason":"Add rollback-safe multi-event commit support for callers already holding the store lock."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/completion.py","reason":"Select the operation read mode, thread the view, and attach the typed completion read basis."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/completion_child_gate.py","reason":"Evaluate child closure from field-level pinned predicates without widening receipts."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py","reason":"Persist the read basis and selected ticket-read mode in completion verdict payloads."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/config.py","reason":"Carry the concrete ticket view through worker dispatch."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/gate_context.py","reason":"Expose the immutable ticket-view context alongside the code snapshot context."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py","reason":"Permit code snapshot capture without full ticket-store materialization and bind the lazy view."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/pai_tools.py","reason":"Serve verifier ticket-tool reads directly from the pinned view."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/relation_snapshot.py","reason":"Compute completion material from pinned field and child-membership predicates."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/runner.py","reason":"Inject the pinned ticket view into the verifier tool set."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py","reason":"Bind criterion-bank stamps to tickets_oid and propagate pinned read failures."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py","reason":"Keep recovery manifest reads fail-closed inside pinned sessions."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_verdict_cache.py","reason":"Bind cached completion verdicts to tickets_oid and reject cross-revision reuse."},{"path":"src/rebar/signing.py","reason":"Prepare completion certificates before publication and verify pinned attestation records."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/completion_bundle.py","reason":"Orchestrate receipt validation, bundle preparation, atomic commit, and delivery."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/completion_candidate.py","reason":"Create UUID-private object-sharing sparse repositories for candidate close commits."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/completion_delivery.py","reason":"Publish candidates with ordinary fast-forward semantics and receipt-aware race recovery."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/completion_txn.py","reason":"Finalize and commit verdict, STATUS, and SIGNATURE as one candidate transaction."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/completion_verifier_run.py","reason":"Keep verifier timing, auto-resume threading, and failure shaping on one call-graph seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/ticket_objects.py","reason":"Provide lazy Git object reads plus pinned resolver and inbound-link indexes."},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/ticket_receipt.py","reason":"Define typed code and ticket OIDs, immutable read bases, and descendant receipt replay."},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/ticket_view.py","reason":"Provide demand-reduced immutable ticket reads and receipt predicate capture."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_close_autoresume_b5f8.py","reason":"Cover view identity and mode propagation across auto-resume."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_close_duration_instrumentation.py","reason":"Cover timing collector threading through the new verifier seam."},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_banking.py","reason":"Cover tickets_oid criterion-bank stamp behavior."},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_verdict_cache.py","reason":"Cover ticket-revision-bound completion cache reuse."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py","reason":"Cover atomic commit faults, idempotence, parallel races, and remote delivery outcomes."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py","reason":"Cover stable lazy reads, resolver parity, receipt replay, hierarchy, links, and fail-closed errors."},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"Refresh the generated env registry after completion config line shifts."},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_sections.py","reason":"Register the rollout key in the core coercion map so configured values are accepted."},{"path":"docs/config-reference.md","reason":"Refresh the generated typed configuration reference for the rollout key."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","14fe-9b7b-c46b-46e0"],["relates_to","1ee2-9704-4f59-45f1"],["relates_to","5866-1024-54af-4fd8"],["relates_to","692a-6b1b-05c8-4d21"],["relates_to","7dea-2f00-db57-4a96"],["relates_to","831f-326d-be85-437a"],["relates_to","aca9-a41d-2449-45b0"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c4050224-bb34-433e-9912-addb638b9948","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["architecture","performance","completion-verifier","concurrency"],"ticket_id":"b03c-f8d4-ef82-4618","ticket_type":"story","title":"Use a lazy pinned ticket view and atomically publish completion-close artifacts","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC5","dd_text":"Pinned ticket-view parity, demand reads, hierarchy/link/global receipt validation, and typed code/ticket roots"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py","dd_id":"AC6-AC10","dd_text":"Short critical section, atomic three-artifact close, rollback faults, races, and remote-CAS disposition"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_standalone_completion_record.py","dd_id":"compat","dd_text":"Existing completion gate and standalone-recording behavior remains compatible"},{"command":"make lint && make typecheck && make test","dd_id":"project-gates","dd_text":"Repository quality and regression gates run in CI because this environment has limited local resources"}]},"source_event_uuids":["b4eda8a9-8193-4716-872f-cb3cd17a095a","39722339-a6fd-43e7-87ec-39d3cde06aa1","c4050224-bb34-433e-9912-addb638b9948","0a8ec3dc-0ae8-4895-8021-ec15ad875266","4be23d6d-4b97-44df-b7fb-bb95c0fb9cee","dca8c8cc-1a2d-40b9-8f70-af5eb5fa27c8","b33fb49d-2c6c-4350-a62f-29002e2b0985","eacbfb40-64dc-4486-8d68-6578be41e2ff","88e10137-45f3-4090-a8fc-ffe6c2ec7cca","e026ad2a-569a-4c34-92e3-6f8676bf8208","c3a34f99-bb44-42f1-a3a4-7434af23835c","5c7acae1-7e16-4eea-9be8-8bfda01041c6","7bae0f1e-be7b-4b32-a951-1d1c0b376393","c6f5ad8a-d7d1-46a0-9f17-ee9c9cc18fb5"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787713804469867001,"uuid":"6d4cd9a6-7f2f-4834-bfb1-3448556d184e"}